4. Participant Summary

A total of 14 participants took part in the study.

User Group	Number of Participants	Percentage
Students	9	64.3%
Non-Teaching Staff	3	21.4%
Teaching Staff	1	7.1%
Visitors	1	7.1%
Total	14	100%
Participant Profile

The majority of respondents were students (64.3%), who are the primary users of university service points and the main target audience for the proposed Virtual Queue Management Mobile Application. The inclusion of teaching staff, non-teaching staff, and visitors provided additional perspectives on queue management challenges and service accessibility.